const PRIVACY = "For the Seedance mobile application (the “App”)\n\nEffective: 19 November 2026   •   Operator: Martin Cermak\n\n> **IMPORTANT**  Text prompts, photos you choose, and the content of your current AI Chat session are sent to external AI providers when you use those features. Saved history on your device is separate from the data processed by those providers.\n\n## Who is responsible for your data\n\nMartin Cermak, an independent individual developer located at C. de Sánchez Pacheco, 49, Chamartín, 28002 Madrid, Spain (“we”, “us”, “our” or “Operator”), operates the App and is the controller of personal data processed for the App to the extent applicable data-protection law assigns that role. You may contact us at martincao@cermak.click for privacy questions or requests.\n\nThis Privacy Policy describes how information is handled when you create AI videos, use AI Chat, manage local history, purchase Premium access or contact support. The App does not require registration or an in-app account.\n\n## Information involved in using the App\n\n### 2.1  Text, images and creative requests\n\nWhen you request an AI video or use prompt-improvement tools, the App may process your text prompts, selected source photos, selected settings (such as video length, size and aspect ratio), and the outputs returned by the AI service. This content is submitted by you for the feature you choose to use. An image can incidentally contain personal data if it depicts identifiable people or includes other identifying information.\n\n### 2.2  AI Chat content\n\nAI Chat can receive your messages and photos selected through the photo picker. Selected images are prepared as JPEG files for transmission to OpenAI. Each new request sends the current chat session’s conversation history, including relevant image attachments, plus the instructions required for the assistant to answer. Other saved chats are not described as being transmitted merely because they are stored on your device.\n\n### 2.3  Generated files and local records\n\nThe App keeps certain user-selected inputs, generated video files, thumbnails, prompts, chat sessions, favorites and related history in its local on-device storage. For example, chat sessions and video history are saved in the App’s Documents storage. Local files are not routinely uploaded to a developer-operated backend, because the App does not have its own backend service.\n\n### 2.4  Purchases and technical identifiers\n\nWhen you purchase or use a subscription, Apple and Apphud may process purchase identifiers, product and transaction details, subscription or entitlement status, and pseudonymous technical identifiers necessary to recognize purchases and prevent misuse. The App also uses a randomly generated installation identifier that may be retained in the device Keychain. Such identifiers are not the same as a registration account or your name, but they may be personal data under applicable law. We do not claim that no identifiers are used.\n\n### 2.5  Support correspondence\n\nIf you contact us by email, we will receive the email address and information you choose to include in your request, and use them to respond and handle the inquiry. We do not require you to provide a contact email address just to use the App.\n\n### 2.6  Network-related information\n\nWhen the App connects to an external AI or purchase service, the provider may automatically receive network and connection information, such as an IP address and request metadata, needed to deliver and protect its service. We do not operate our own backend server to keep corresponding user request logs.\n\n## How AI processing works\n\nAI video generation uses PixVerse V6 through fal.ai. The text prompt and, for image-to-video requests, the selected photo are transferred to fal.ai for processing. The resulting video is made available through a provider-hosted URL, then downloaded and stored as a local file on your device for playback and history.\n\nAI Chat uses OpenAI GPT-4o-mini for prompt assistance and conversational responses. The content transmitted includes the current message, any attached images and the earlier messages in that chat session. AI-based prompt enhancement may likewise involve an external text-processing service as required by the chosen feature.\n\nThese transmissions are necessary for the user-requested AI features; the app cannot perform the same third-party AI generation entirely offline. Please avoid uploading private, confidential or sensitive material you do not want an external provider to process.\n\n## Why we process data and the legal basis\n\nWhere the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) or similar law applies, our legal bases depend on the processing activity:\n\n- Providing requested video generation, AI Chat, local history and subscription access: performance of our contract with you (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR), where applicable.\n- Responding to support inquiries, maintaining service security and investigating misuse: our legitimate interests in operating and protecting the App and assisting users (Article 6(1)(f)), unless another basis is more appropriate.\n- Meeting mandatory legal, consumer-protection or accounting obligations, if relevant: compliance with a legal obligation (Article 6(1)(c)).\n- Processing that applicable law requires to be based on your consent: consent (Article 6(1)(a)), which you may withdraw where applicable, without affecting processing that was lawful before withdrawal.\n\nDevice permission prompts and voluntary selection of images control access to your photos or camera; the precise legal basis for processing personal data is assessed separately from the operating-system permission itself.\n\n## Service providers and recipients\n\nWe share or facilitate transfer of information only as needed to provide selected features, manage purchases, respond to requests or meet legal obligations. The main services involved are:\n\n- fal.ai (AI video generation): receives video prompts, selected photos and related request parameters; returns generated results and hosts generated files at least during delivery.\n- OpenAI (AI Chat and relevant text assistance): receives messages, the current chat-session context, selected image attachments and associated request information.\n- Apple (App Store and In-App Purchase): handles Apple account billing, purchase confirmations, renewals, cancellations, refunds and related payment processes under Apple’s terms.\n- Apphud (subscription management): processes purchase and subscription status and the technical identifiers necessary to manage entitlements and related purchase reporting.\n\nWe do not provide a public gallery or in-app user-to-user messaging service. The App is not configured to run advertising campaigns based on an advertising identifier, and it does not use a separate Firebase analytics or third-party crash-reporting service. Apphud may provide purchase-related reporting as part of its normal subscription-management functions.\n\nIf you choose to share or export content to another service, you control the destination and that recipient may process the shared material under its own rules. We may also disclose data where genuinely required by applicable law or to establish or defend legal claims.\n\n## Local storage and device permissions\n\nChat sessions, generated videos, source images and thumbnails are saved in the App’s local Documents storage (including app folders for chat sessions, videos, thumbnails and sources). The App uses device storage rather than a developer-operated cloud gallery to provide history and playback.\n\n- Photos access or the system photo picker: lets you choose images for generation or for AI Chat attachments.\n- Camera: lets you capture source photographs for supported creative features.\n- Add to Photos: lets you save generated videos to your device photo library when you choose to do so.\n\nYou may manage relevant permissions in your device Settings. Denying a permission can prevent features requiring that access from working, but it does not prevent use of unrelated App features.\n\n## Retention and deletion\n\n### 7.1  Data saved on your device\n\nLocal history and chat content generally remain available until you remove them using the relevant in-app controls or uninstall the App. You can delete individual videos or clear video history in History, and can select and delete multiple chats with confirmation. There is currently no single “Delete all data” option in the App Settings.\n\nUninstalling the App ordinarily removes files stored in its Documents directory. An installation UUID stored in the device Keychain may remain after the App is deleted, depending on device and operating-system behavior. Copies that you previously exported or saved in your photo library are not removed by deleting an in-app history item.\n\n### 7.2  Data handled by external providers\n\nAI processing requires transmission to fal.ai and/or OpenAI. Those services may retain submitted prompts, uploaded photos, chat requests, outputs or related records for periods determined by their contractual settings, service rules and applicable law. We do not represent that our in-app deletion tools also remove information from those providers. In particular, we have not established a fixed retention period for content uploaded to or generated through fal.ai, and the App does not provide a direct deletion control for that provider’s stored media.\n\nApple and Apphud may retain purchase records and related identifiers under their own legal, financial and service requirements. Deleting the App does not automatically cancel your Apple subscription or erase records kept by those providers. Support emails may be retained as reasonably needed to answer inquiries, resolve disputes and comply with law.\n\n## Security and confidentiality\n\nWe seek to limit processing to the information needed for the requested functions and rely on operating-system safeguards, local device storage and third-party service protections. Nevertheless, no device, network connection or service can guarantee absolute security. Keep your device secure and avoid sending secrets or sensitive personal information in AI prompts or chat messages.\n\n## International processing and transfers\n\nAI and purchase-service providers may process information in countries outside Spain or the European Economic Area, including the United States. Where international data-transfer restrictions apply, processing must rely on an applicable lawful transfer mechanism or safeguard, depending on the provider and the specific processing. You may request additional information through the contact details below, and you can review the applicable providers’ disclosures.\n\n## Your choices and privacy rights\n\nDepending on your location and applicable law, you may have rights to request access to, correction or erasure of personal data, to restrict or object to certain processing, to receive portable copies of eligible information and to withdraw consent where consent is used. These rights are subject to legal exceptions and reasonable identity verification.\n\nYou can remove local videos and chats through their in-app controls and control photo and camera permissions through your device. For privacy requests regarding processing for which we are responsible, email martincao@cermak.click. We will review and respond as required by applicable law. Where a provider independently controls data, requests may also need to be directed to that provider.\n\nIf you are in the EEA, you may also complain to a competent data-protection supervisory authority, including the Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD), subject to applicable rules. You do not need to contact us before filing a complaint.\n\n## Age and protection of younger users\n\nThe App is intended for users aged 16 and over, subject to any higher minimum age required by applicable law. It is not designed for children younger than 16. We do not knowingly seek personal information from children under that age. If you believe a child under the applicable minimum age has supplied information through the App, please contact us.\n\n## Brand authorization and independence\n\nUse of the SEEDANCE name and applicable brand assets in the App is authorized under a signed Brand Authorization and Trademark License Agreement dated 5 November 2026 between Spring Technology Services Ltd. and Martin Cermak. The App is independently operated by Martin Cermak, not directly by Spring Technology Services Ltd. or ByteDance.\n\nThe brand-authorization relationship does not, by itself, mean that your prompts, images, chats, purchases or other App information are sent to the brand owner. Information is handled as described in this Policy according to the App’s actual technical integrations.\n\n## Third-party privacy information\n\nThe following official resources provide additional information about the principal service providers. Their policies and technical controls can change, and specific processing may also be governed by business service agreements:\n\n- [fal.ai Privacy Policy](https://fal.ai/legal/privacy-policy)\n- [fal.ai Media Retention Documentation](https://fal.ai/docs/documentation/model-apis/media-expiration)\n- [OpenAI Privacy Information](https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/)\n- [OpenAI API Data Controls](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data)\n- [Apphud Privacy Policy](https://legal.apphud.com/privacy)\n- [Apple Privacy Policy](https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/en-ww/)\n\n## Changes to this Policy\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy when App features, service providers, legal requirements or data practices change. The updated policy will be made accessible in the App and will indicate its effective date. Where the law requires additional notice or consent, we will provide it.\n\n## Contact\n\nData controller / App Operator: Martin Cermak (individual developer)\nPostal address: C. de Sánchez Pacheco, 49, Chamartín, 28002 Madrid, Spain\nPrivacy and support email: martincao@cermak.click";

const TERMS = "For the Seedance mobile application (the “App”)\n\nEffective: 19 November 2026   •   Operator: Martin Cermak\n\n> **PLEASE READ**  These Terms govern your use of the App, including AI video generation, AI Chat, and paid features. Your purchases are billed through Apple.\n\n## Operator and acceptance\n\nThese Terms of Use (“Terms”) form an agreement between you and Martin Cermak, an independent individual developer based at C. de Sánchez Pacheco, 49, Chamartín, 28002 Madrid, Spain (“we”, “us”, “our” or “Operator”). They govern your download of, access to, and use of the App and its related features.\n\nBy accessing or using the App, you agree to these Terms and the accompanying Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, do not use the App. Any mandatory rights granted to you by applicable consumer or data-protection law remain unaffected.\n\n## Eligibility and age requirement\n\nThe App is intended for individuals aged 16 or older. You must also meet any higher minimum age required by the laws applicable to you. Where applicable, users who have not reached the age of legal majority must obtain permission from a parent or legal guardian. Do not use the App where use is prohibited by law.\n\n## Service description\n\nThe App offers creative tools that may include text-to-video generation, image-to-video generation, templates and styles, prompt enhancement, video settings (such as resolution, duration and aspect ratio), AI Chat for prompt assistance, a local generation history, saved favorites, and options to reuse prompts, download, save or share generated content.\n\nThe App uses third-party artificial intelligence technology, including video-generation functionality provided through fal.ai (PixVerse V6) and text-based assistance provided through OpenAI (GPT-4o-mini). We may change or replace supported models, features, limits and technical configurations as the service develops. Availability, processing time and output quality can vary.\n\n## Limited license to use the App\n\nSubject to these Terms, we grant you a personal, limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable and revocable license to use the App on devices you own or control, in accordance with applicable Apple usage rules. The App is licensed to you, not sold. You may not copy, reverse engineer, distribute, sublicense or commercially exploit the App itself except to the extent permitted by law or with our prior written permission.\n\n## Your inputs, images and generated content\n\nYou retain any rights you already hold in text prompts, photographs and other material that you submit (“Inputs”). You confirm that you have the necessary rights and permissions to provide those Inputs for AI processing, including the appropriate consent when images show identifiable people, and that your use does not infringe any third-party rights.\n\nBy requesting a generation or AI Chat response, you instruct the App to transmit the Inputs and relevant conversational context to the applicable AI service solely to perform the feature requested. Your Inputs may be processed by the relevant third-party service under its applicable terms, policies and legal arrangements.\n\nGenerated images, videos, text and other results (“Outputs”) are algorithmically produced. Rights in Outputs depend on applicable law and any relevant third-party terms; copyrightability, originality, exclusivity and freedom from third-party claims are not guaranteed. Similar Outputs may be generated for other people. You are responsible for reviewing Outputs before using or sharing them, including obtaining necessary permissions for likenesses, copyrighted works and other protected material.\n\n## AI Chat and prompt assistance\n\nAI Chat is designed to assist with concepts and video prompts. It may accept text and selected images. For each message, the App sends the content of the current conversation session, including relevant attachments, to OpenAI along with instructions needed to provide the response. Chats are stored locally within the App, subject to the processing described in the Privacy Policy.\n\nAI responses may be mistaken, incomplete or unsuitable for a specific use. Do not rely on them as professional, legal, financial, medical or safety advice. AI Chat currently requires an active Premium subscription.\n\n## Prohibited conduct and content\n\nYou must use the App lawfully and responsibly. In particular, you must not use, attempt to use or deliberately circumvent the App or its safeguards to:\n\n- Create, request or distribute child sexual abuse material, sexual exploitation, pornographic or sexually explicit content, or any other content prohibited by applicable law or service policies.\n- Generate non-consensual intimate imagery, exploit another person’s likeness, impersonate individuals deceptively, or violate privacy, publicity or intellectual-property rights.\n- Promote unlawful violence, harassment, hate, exploitation, fraud, dangerous wrongdoing or otherwise harmful or abusive conduct.\n- Interfere with the service, abuse technical limits, attempt unauthorized access, or bypass filters, purchase controls or protective measures.\n\nThe App is not intended to enable pornographic or otherwise prohibited generation. AI-provider safeguards or service rules may block requests or refuse to generate Outputs. No filtering system is guaranteed to identify every harmful request or result. We may restrict functionality where necessary to comply with law, provider requirements or these Terms.\n\n## Subscriptions, purchases and billing\n\nSome App functions, including AI Chat, require Premium access. The App currently offers paid auto-renewable subscriptions through Apple In-App Purchase, with subscription status and entitlement management supported by Apphud. A free trial or a one-time purchase is not currently offered; if such options are introduced in the future, their availability and specific terms will be displayed before purchase.\n\n- The subscription term, included features, applicable price, currency and renewal conditions are presented on the purchase screen before you confirm payment.\n- An auto-renewable subscription renews at the end of each billing period unless you cancel it in your Apple subscription settings before renewal. Cancellation ordinarily stops future renewal and does not immediately remove benefits already paid for.\n- Apple processes payments and manages billing, cancellations and purchase refunds under its applicable policies and mandatory consumer law. We do not receive your full payment-card details.\n- If trials, introductory pricing or one-time purchases become available later, the offer shown in the App Store or purchase screen will govern that transaction, including eligibility and any conversion to a paid subscription.\n\nYou can manage or cancel subscriptions through your Apple account (Settings → Apple Account → Subscriptions). Purchase restoration is subject to Apple’s purchase records and the features made available in the App. We may reasonably change subscription offerings prospectively, subject to notice and applicable law.\n\n## Local storage, privacy and sharing\n\nThe App does not require user registration. History, saved generated videos, source images and AI Chat sessions are stored locally on your device. Videos may be generated by a third-party service, retrieved from a provider URL and then saved locally. Local storage does not mean that AI requests are processed only on your device.\n\nYou can delete videos or clear history through the available History controls and delete chats through the chat interface. Removing the App generally removes its local document files, but some installation identifiers stored in the device Keychain may persist. Deleting local content does not automatically delete copies or records already held by third-party AI or purchase service providers. For details, see the Privacy Policy.\n\nWhen you choose to share or export an Output to another app, website or person, the recipient’s own terms and privacy practices may apply. You are responsible for what you decide to publish or transmit.\n\n## Brand authorization and intellectual property\n\nThe SEEDANCE name, logo and other authorized brand elements are used pursuant to a signed Brand Authorization and Trademark License Agreement between Spring Technology Services Ltd. and Martin Cermak, dated 5 November 2026. The authorization concerns use of the brand in connection with this independently developed App; it does not transfer ownership of the brand to us.\n\nThe App is independently developed, distributed and supported by Martin Cermak. The brand authorization does not make the App an official ByteDance product and does not mean that Spring Technology Services Ltd. or ByteDance operates, endorses or guarantees the App or its AI functionality. No ownership rights in the SEEDANCE trademark or other protected brand assets are granted to App users.\n\nExcept for Inputs and Outputs to the extent permitted by applicable law, the App, its interface, original software, text and other protected materials are owned by or licensed to the Operator or relevant rights holders. All ungranted rights are reserved.\n\n## Third-party services\n\nThe App depends on external services and operating-system features, including fal.ai, OpenAI, Apple In-App Purchase and Apphud. Those providers may impose their own technical limits, acceptable-use requirements and privacy practices. Service outages, changes to provider policies or model availability may affect generation and other App functions. The Operator does not control third-party infrastructure or data-retention policies.\n\n## Availability, safety and warranties\n\nWe aim to keep the App available and usable, but we do not guarantee uninterrupted access, any particular generation speed or resolution, or that an Output will meet your expectations. To the maximum extent permitted by law, the App and its AI features are provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties beyond those that cannot lawfully be excluded. Nothing in these Terms removes your mandatory statutory consumer remedies.\n\n## Liability\n\nTo the extent permitted by applicable law, we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, loss of anticipated profits or loss arising from your reliance on inaccurate AI Outputs, unlawful Inputs, a third-party outage, or a sharing decision you control. These limits do not apply to liability that cannot legally be excluded, including liability for intentional misconduct, gross negligence where exclusion is prohibited, or mandatory consumer protections. Your rights under applicable law take precedence over any conflicting clause.\n\n## Suspension and termination\n\nYou may stop using the App at any time and cancel any active subscription through Apple. Uninstalling the App does not cancel an Apple subscription. We may suspend or discontinue access to some features where reasonably necessary for safety, compliance, misuse prevention, technical changes or termination of a third-party service, subject to applicable law and any rights related to prepaid services.\n\n## Changes to these Terms\n\nWe may update these Terms to reflect changes in functionality, applicable law, provider requirements or business practices. The latest version will be accessible in the App. We will provide additional notice of material changes where required by law. Continued use after an effective update constitutes acceptance only where allowed by applicable law; otherwise, any required consent will be obtained.\n\n## Applicable law and consumer rights\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of Spain, without depriving consumers of mandatory protections under the law of their country of habitual residence where applicable. Any dispute will be handled by courts having jurisdiction under applicable consumer-protection and procedural law. We encourage you to contact us first so we can try to resolve issues directly.\n\n## Apple-related terms\n\nThese Terms are between you and Martin Cermak, not Apple. Apple is not responsible for the App or its contents and has no obligation to provide maintenance or support for it. To the extent applicable, Apple is not responsible for addressing claims regarding the App, including product liability, regulatory compliance or third-party intellectual-property infringement; those matters are the Operator’s responsibility as required by law. You agree to comply with applicable Apple usage rules. Apple and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms and may enforce the relevant provisions against you.\n\n## Contact\n\nOperator: Martin Cermak (individual developer)\nPostal address: C. de Sánchez Pacheco, 49, Chamartín, 28002 Madrid, Spain\nSupport and legal inquiries: martincao@cermak.click";

